Explanation of the change:

- We still keep the original bounds normalization.
- Immediately after setting `bounds`, we interpret them as real `Date` objects (`fromDate`/`toDate`).
- If the current `reference` (the month the calendar is displaying) lies before `fromDate` or after `toDate`, we reset it to the nearest bound and fire `onReference` so that the parent gets notified.
- By clamping the reference here, the users will never be able to navigate or select dates outside of your `calendarProps.bounds`.
